---
import "../styles/global.css";

import MainLayout from "../layouts/Main.astro";
import { Image } from "@unpic/astro";
import Navbar from "../partials/Navbar.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/Eyebrow.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";

import HeroBackground from "../assets/piltover-arcane.webp";
import FirstIter from "../assets/poroscout-first-iter.webp";
import OldLogo from "../assets/poroscout-old-logo.webp";
import PoroIdentity from "../assets/poroscout-identity.webp";
import PoroMoba from "../assets/poroscout-moba-email.webp";
---

<MainLayout
  content={{
    title: "PoroScout - About",
    description:
      "Learn about PoroScout, the League of Legends Discord bot, and the story behind it.",
  }}
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="relative">
    <Image
      src={HeroBackground}
      alt="Piltover background"
      height={1200}
      priority
      placeholder="lqip"
      unstyled
      class="w-full h-[70vh] min-h-[480px] object-cover opacity-65"
    />

    <!-- fade to black -->
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-black/30 to-gray-950 from-70%"
    >
    </div>

    <div class="absolute inset-0 flex flex-col h-[70vh] min-h-[480px]">
      <Navbar class="z-50" />

      <div
        class="flex grow flex-col justify-center max-w-7xl w-full mx-auto text-primary font-display px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"
      >
        <h2
          class="text-base sm:text-lg font-semibold uppercase text-grey-1 tracking-widest"
        >
          Piltover's Finest
        </h2>
        <h1
          class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-black mb-4 text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-b from-primary to-gray-400 from-70% leading-[1.125]"
        >
          About PoroScout
        </h1>
        <p class="max-w-2xl font-body text-sm sm:text-base text-grey-1">
          The League of Legends scouting party that lives in your Discord
          server.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- What PoroScout is -->
  <section class="bg-gray-950">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24">
      <Eyebrow>What it is</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="mt-3 mb-6 font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-gold-1">
        Pro-grade League data, inside Discord
      </h2>
      <div
        class="space-y-5 font-body text-base sm:text-lg text-grey-1 leading-relaxed [&_a]:text-gold-2 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-2 [&_a]:transition-colors [&_a:hover]:text-hex-teal"
      >
        <p>
          PoroScout is a League of Legends Discord bot that brings champion
          builds, ranked tracking, match breakdowns, and patch notes straight
          into the servers and DMs where you and your squad already hang out. No
          browser tabs, no alt-tabbing, just type
          <code class="text-hex-teal">/</code> and scout. PoroScout's goal is to facilitate
          easier conversations about champions or your own performance within Discord.
        </p>
        <p>
          Look up any summoner, lock in the optimal build before champ select,
          break down a friend's last game, show off your wonderful performance,
          or defend your inting Sion game. The data is accurate and up to date,
          pulled from sources like the Riot Games API and Mobalytics, and served
          back to you in seconds.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why -->
  <section class="bg-hex-blue-deep">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24">
      <Eyebrow>Why it exists</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="mt-3 mb-6 font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-gold-1">
        Built by a player, for players
      </h2>
      <div
        class="space-y-5 font-body text-base sm:text-lg text-grey-1 leading-relaxed [&_a]:text-gold-2 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-2 [&_a]:transition-colors [&_a:hover]:text-hex-teal"
      >
        <p>
          PoroScout was born in 2021, my freshman year of High School. My
          friends and I participated in highschool level League tournaments,
          playing teams from around the state. Our main communication channel?
          Discord. When it came to scouting our next players, we'd often share
          OP.GG links in chat, and constantly have to switch in and out from
          Discord.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the time, an alternative bot did exist, but it was heavily
          out-of-date and did not provide reliable information on champions. So,
          one night, I started the work on developing PoroScout, and before
          long, PoroScout said its first words!
        </p>

        <Image
          src={FirstIter}
          alt="Screenshot from 2021 of PoroScout's /profile command."
        />

        <p>
          One of my friends, <a href="https://bardman.dev">Daniel</a> helped give
          PoroScout it's identity:
        </p>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2">
          <Image
            src={PoroIdentity}
            alt="The origins of the Piltover theme, as a random conversation on Discord."
          />

          <Image
            src={OldLogo}
            alt="PoroScout's first logo, put together from three elements: League background, binoculars, and a Poro."
          />
        </div>

        <p>
          Before long, PoroScout had all of it's basic commands implemented, but
          there was one hurdle: providing Champion statistics. Riot's API
          provides an easy way to fetch player statistics, but does not provide
          any form of champion statistics.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is why if you go between stat sites, like Mobalytics to U.GG to
          leagueofgraphs, you will find differences in the data they report for
          champions. This data must be collected by each site and aggregated.
        </p>
        <p>
          I had coded up my own scraping system. It started from a single
          player, collected data on their match history, then for each player
          that they played with, it would scan deeper into those new players'
          match history. After letting it run overnight, collecting thousands of
          matches, I took a look at the data.
        </p>
        <p>
          It was all garbage. Turns out, with the amount of champions League
          has, you need <i>a lot</i> of data to make good generalizations (such as
          item builds, counters, winrates). So, I pivoted. Why re-invent the wheel
          when all of these companies already have data. At the time, I used the Mobalytics
          overlay to help with item builds, so I sent a cold email out to one of the
          Mobalytics founders. And before you know it, I got a response!
        </p>

        <Image
          src={PoroMoba}
          alt="Email response from Mobalytic's co-founder Bogdan giving the greenlight for PoroScout!"
        />

        <p>
          From there, I kept growing PoroScout. Contacting many Discord server
          administrators to expand PoroScout coverage and build new features.
        </p>

        <p>
          What you're using today is the third iteration of that idea, rebuilt
          from to be faster, cleaner, and lighter than ever. It's an independent
          project, made and maintained because tracking the climb and scouting
          the enemy team should be effortless for your whole server, not just
          the one person with the stats site open.
        </p>
        <p>
          P.S. If you read this far, and want to support the project, a <a
            href="https://github.com/sponsors/ItzDerock">small donation</a
          > would be greatly appreciated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</MainLayout>
